  "notes": "One date per Employment Situation (nonfarm payrolls) news release (8:30 a.m. ET), as published by the BLS release schedule; archive filenames (empsit_MMDDYYYY) encode the actual release day. Usually the first Friday of the month, but never assumed: irregular dates (e.g. 2017-03-10, 2017-12-08, 2021-10-08, 2023-03-10, 2026-02-11) were verified individually. 2025 has 11 dates: no release on the first Fridays of October or November (2025 lapse in appropriations); September data was released 2025-11-20 and October+November data together on 2025-12-16 — one release date. Coverage ends 2026-09-04 — the last release BLS's published schedule confirms that we could verify; later 2026 dates exist on the BLS schedule but were not independently verifiable from this build environment, so they are omitted rather than guessed. Verified 2026-08-25 via search extracts of official BLS pages (direct fetch of bls.gov was unavailable); dates after 2026-08-25 are scheduled, not yet released.",
